{"id":84627,"docketId":1277617,"caseName":"Phillips v. Hyde","caseNameFull":"Phillips v. Hyde","slug":"phillips-v-hyde","docketNumber":"","dateFiled":"1789-06-01","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1789,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":"<p>\nVerdict on replevin-bond.\n</p> <p>Debt upon a replevin-bond, after judgment de retorno h\u00e1bendo in the replevin, and thereupon, a return of elongatur.</p>","proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Sergeant,\n, \n*Levy,\n, Sergeant, in reply,","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":8,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":84627,"type":"majority","typeCode":"010combined","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1582,"isHtml":true,"text":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n<opinion data-order=\"9\" data-type=\"opinion\" id=\"x999-1\" type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"b472-8\">\n  The Court\n </author>\n<p id=\"A3v\">\n  overruled the evidence,\n  <a class=\"footnote\" href=\"#fn(a)\" id=\"fn(a)_ref\">\n   (a)\n  </a>\n</p>\n<p id=\"b472-9\">\n  A question then arose, whether the jury could include the costs which had accrued on the replevin, in their verdict in the present action. And the Court were clearly of opinion, that they could, and ought to do so.\n  <a class=\"footnote\" href=\"#fn(b)\" id=\"fn(b)_ref\">\n<em>\n    (b)\n   </em>\n</a>\n</p>\n<p id=\"b472-10\">\n  Conformable to which was the verdict of the jury.\n </p>\n\n\n<div class=\"footnotes\"><div class=\"footnote\" id=\"fn(a)\" label=\"(a)\">\n<a class=\"footnote\" href=\"#fn(a)_ref\">\n   (a)\n  </a>\n<p id=\"b472-16\">\n<em>\n</em>\n   See Shewoll v. Fell; <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"6309234\"><a href=\"/opinion/6437191/shewel-v-fell/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Shewel v. Fell\">3 Yeates 17</a></span>; 4 <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"6309234\"><a href=\"/opinion/6437191/shewel-v-fell/#47\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Shewel v. Fell\">Id. 47</a></span>.\n  </p>\n</div><div class=\"footnote\" id=\"fn(b)\" label=\"(b)\">\n<a class=\"footnote\" href=\"#fn(b)_ref\">\n   (b)\n  </a>\n<p id=\"b472-17\">\n<em>\n    Sergeant\n   </em>\n   having suggested, that both the points in this case had been otherwise determined in a case of Jackson\n   <em>\n    v.\n   </em>\n   Webb, Mr. President Shippen said, that the matter was there left, upon equitable circumstances, to the court.\n  </p>\n</div></div></opinion>"}],"citations":[]}